+# Result Claim Audit before Letta passage persistence
+
+This example targets Letta's current `PassageManager` write methods:
+
+- `create_agent_passage_async`
+- `create_source_passage_async`
+
+The wrapper runs before `ArchivalPassage.create_async` or
+`SourcePassage.create_async`. Accepted receipts are stored in the existing
+`Passage.metadata_` mapping that PassageManager already copies into its ORM
+objects, so no migration is required.
+
+```python
+from letta.services.passage_manager import PassageManager
+from letta_result_claim_audit import ResultClaimAuditedPassageManager
+
+passages = ResultClaimAuditedPassageManager(PassageManager())
+created = await passages.create_agent_passage_async(
+    passage,
+    actor,
+    provenance={
+        "trust": "quarantined",
+        "origin": "retrieval",
+        "actor_kind": "rag_document",
+        "source_record_id": "doc-42",
+        "source_ref": "s3://bucket/doc-42",
+    },
+)
+```
+
+The integration fails closed on missing provenance, audit outage, malformed
+output, or non-result verdict before the wrapped manager receives the passage.
+
+Runnable adapter and isolated tests:
+
+https://github.com/AInoAKARI/keymaster-mcp/tree/main/integrations/letta-result-claim-audit
+
+Apply this patch:
+
+```bash
+curl -L https://raw.githubusercontent.com/AInoAKARI/keymaster-mcp/main/patches/letta-ai-letta-result-claim-audit.patch | git apply
+```
+
+Verification: `python -m unittest -v test_letta_result_claim_audit.py` — three
+tests cover accepted receipt persistence, missing provenance, and rejected
+verdict without installing Letta or calling the network.
